'''When the number of overt sumti exceeds the number of sumti places''': see ((SE + x2-less brivla)) for the proposal that a nonce selbri-meaning is created that has a place structure that accommodates all overt sumti.

'''When the number of sumti places exceeds the number of overt sumti''': the current official rule is:
;:Empty places are to be filled only by implicit ''zo'e''.
;:''zo'e'' can be construed as anything but ''no da'' and ''zi'o''.
In usage, though, the rule is:
;:Empty places are to be filled only by implicit ''zo'e'' or implicit ''zi'o''.
Xorxes has proposed (and I increasingly like the idea) that the rule should be:
;:Empty places are to be filled only by implicit ''zi'o''.

Maybe I'll spell out the attractions of this when I have more time, but in the meantime I table it here for comment. --((And))
